                <p>Welcome to the definitive online directory of watchmaking businesses based in America: watch brands, independent watchmakers, and the suppliers and repairers around them, plus a few of our Canadian neighbors. We list them whether they make their products here, abroad or both. We don't judge what counts as American made; we report what each brand says about where its products are made.</p>
                <p>Our mission is simple: to increase visibility for American watch businesses, foster collaboration, and help drive a new golden era for domestic watchmaking. From independent artisans crafting one-of-a-kind pieces to established brands rooted in tradition, we bring together the full spectrum of talent and innovation in one place.</p>

                <h2>What the directory is for</h2>
                <div class="aims">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>Visibility &amp; marketing</h3>
                        <p>We help watchmakers reach new audiences and grow their brand through enhanced online exposure.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>Customer engagement &amp; lead generation</h3>
                        <p>Whether you're a collector, enthusiast, or first-time buyer, our directory makes it easy to discover and connect with American watch brands and makers that align with your interests.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>Supporting recruitment &amp; supply chains</h3>
                        <p>We help watchmakers find skilled talent and reliable parts and accessories suppliers to strengthen the backbone of American horology.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2>Who we are</h2>
                <p>The American Watchmaking Directory is a wholly volunteer-driven initiative created and maintained by two passionate watch enthusiasts in Seattle, Washington.</p>
                <h3>Hamza</h3>
                <p>Head of Partnerships at WatchCharts. One of the chapter heads, RedBar Seattle.</p>
                <h3>Vivek</h3>
                <p>Software Development Engineer at Expedia.</p>

                <h2>What's up next</h2>
                <p>There's lots to do. Here's what's currently next on our to-do list, until we get sufficient feedback convincing us to invest in something else first.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Add structured info on specific attributes (watchmaker, strapmaker, dial maker, etc).</li>
                    <li>Brand outreach to confirm current information and contribute information on what they make in America.</li>
                    <li>(Early user feedback) Tag brands by mechanical/quartz movements.</li>
                </ul>

